how to implement this logic here:
How a received message becomes a clickable @mention
Step 1 — Parse HTML into attributed string
AttributedStringBuilder.swift:83-111

The HTML (formatted_body) is parsed with SwiftSoup (not a WebView, for security). <a href="https://matrix.to/#/@john:server.org">John</a> becomes a span with a .link attribute pointing to the matrix.to URL.

Step 2 — Scan plain text for bare mentions
AttributedStringBuilder.swift:305-401

addLinksAndMentions() runs regexes from MatrixEntityRegex against the plain string:

userIdentifierRegex — finds @user:server.org patterns
roomAliasRegex — finds #room:server.org
allUsersRegex — finds @room
Any matches that don't already have a .link attribute get one added (user IDs get a matrix.to permalink).

Step 3 — Convert links to mention pills
AttributedStringBuilder.swift:404-431

addMatrixEntityPermalinkAttributesTo() enumerates all .link attributes, calls parseMatrixEntityFrom(uri:) on each URL, and routes to MentionBuilder:


case .user(let userID):
    mentionBuilder.handleUserMention(for: attributedString, in: range, url: url, userID: userID, ...)
MentionBuilder replaces the text range with a PillTextAttachment (a custom NSTextAttachment that renders a styled chip with avatar + name).

Step 4 — Render and handle taps
MessageText.swift:58-175

The attributed string is rendered in MessageTextView (a UITextView wrapping, using TextKit 1 — required for custom text attachments). Taps on links are caught by the UITextViewDelegate:


func textView(_ textView, primaryActionFor textItem, defaultAction) -> UIAction? {
    if case .link(let url) = textItem.content {
        // fires openURL — which routes matrix.to permalinks to the user profile screen
        self?.openURLAction.callAsFunction(url)
    }
}
React Native equivalent
You don't have NSTextAttachment, so the approach is:

Parse the HTML formatted_body — use a library like react-native-render-html which handles <a> tags and lets you override renderers.

Custom renderer for <a> tags — detect matrix.to links and render a styled <Text> chip instead of a plain link:


const renderers = {
  a: ({ TDefaultRenderer, tnode, ...props }) => {
    const href = tnode.attributes.href ?? '';
    const entity = parseMatrixEntity(href); // your parser
    if (entity?.type === 'user') {
      return (
        <TouchableOpacity onPress={() => openUserProfile(entity.userId)}>
          <Text style={styles.mentionPill}>@{tnode.children[0]?.data}</Text>
        </TouchableOpacity>
      );
    }
    return <TDefaultRenderer tnode={tnode} {...props} />;
  }
};

<RenderHtml source={{ html: formattedBody }} renderers={renderers} />
For plain text — run a regex for @user:server patterns on the body field and split into segments, rendering matches as tappable <Text> spans (same ghost-text trick as before).

On tap — the matrix.to URL tells you the user ID. Navigate to a profile screen or show a bottom sheet with that user's info.

